#: gui/main.c:2497
msgid "deleted"
msgstr "eliminado"

#: gui/main.c:2498
msgid "not backed up"
msgstr "sin copia"

#: gui/main.c:2499
msgid "drive not plugged in"
msgstr "unidad no conectada"

#: gui/main.c:2507
msgid ""
"How the list of files shows each one:\r\n"
"    Name: a good copy is on a drive that is plugged in.\r\n"
"    Name   on <drive>, in italics: its copy is on a drive that is not plugged in.\r\n"
"    Name   - not backed up, in italics: it has no copy yet.\r\n"
"    Name   - changed since backup, in another colour: only an older version is backed up.\r\n"
"    Name   - copy damaged, in bold: the copy on the plugged-in drive is missing or damaged; back up again to fix it.\r\n"
"    Name   - deleted, struck through: gone from its folder; BRODALF still keeps track of its copies.\r\n"
"    Folder   (3 of 10 available): how many files in it have a good copy on a plugged-in drive.\r\n"
"    ★ starred: also copied to your extra places. [encrypted]: encrypted on every drive and extra place it is copied to."
msgstr ""
"Cómo muestra la lista de archivos cada uno:\r\n"
"    Nombre: hay una copia buena en una unidad conectada.\r\n"
"    Nombre   en <unidad>, en cursiva: su copia está en una unidad que no está conectada.\r\n"
"    Nombre   - sin copia, en cursiva: aún no tiene copia.\r\n"
"    Nombre   - cambiado desde la copia, en otro color: solo hay copia de una versión anterior.\r\n"
"    Nombre   - copia dañada, en negrita: la copia de la unidad conectada falta o está dañada; vuelve a hacer la copia para arreglarlo.\r\n"
"    Nombre   - eliminado, tachado: ya no está en su carpeta; BRODALF sigue controlando sus copias.\r\n"
